[00:07.86]A: I used to rule the world
[00:11.55]B: Seas would rise when I gave the word
[00:14.03]A: Now in the morning, I sleep alone
[00:18.35]B: Sweep the streets I used to own
[00:35.34]A: I used to roll the dice
[00:39.40]B: Feel the fear in my enemy's eyes
[00:42.66]A: Listened as the crowd would sing
[00:46.47]AB: "Now the old king is dead, long live the king"
[00:49.31]A: One minute I held the key
[00:53.28]B: Next, the walls were closed on me
[00:55.95]A: And I discovered that my castles stand
[01:00.21]B: Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand
[01:04.03]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[01:07.91]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[01:11.37]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[01:14.49]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[01:18.29]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[01:21.69]B: Once you'd gone, there was never
[01:24.32]A: Never an honest word
[01:28.03]AB: And that was when I ruled the world
[01:44.68]A: It was a wicked and wild wind
[01:48.85]B: Blew down the doors to let me in
[01:51.54]A: Shattered windows and the sound of drums
[01:55.90]B: People couldn't believe what I'd become
[01:59.09]A: Revolutionaries wait
[02:02.93]B: For my head on a silver plate
[02:05.38]A: Just a puppet on a lonely string
[02:09.95]B: Oh, who would ever want to be king?
[02:13.72]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[02:17.32]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[02:20.73]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[02:24.19]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[02:27.67]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[02:31.25]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[02:34.44]A: Never an honest word
[02:37.51]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
[03:09.85]AB: Hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[03:12.90]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[03:16.48]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[03:19.76]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[03:23.38]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[03:26.84]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[03:29.98]A: Never an honest word
[03:33.22]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
